-- title:
--   Supersingular point of the finite chart of X₀(Mp) is closed with finite residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for the set $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p)))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield generated over $L$ by the image under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by all quotients $f/g$ of $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ having integral $q$-expansions, with $g \neq 0$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$, and let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular $j$-function, assumed nonzero. Write $B =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} B$, i.e. a prime ideal of $B$, such that the image of $\varpi$ lies in $y$ and such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon B \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p \Omega`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Then $y$ is a maximal ideal of $B$ and the quotient $B/y$ is finite.
--
--   This says that a point of the special fibre at $\varpi$ of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model attached to $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ whose $j$-invariant is supersingular is a closed point with finite residue field; the proof combines finite generation of the chart algebra over $A$ with Zariski's lemma. It is used in the analysis of the completed local rings of the model at such points, namely in the statements producing a complete discrete valuation ring mapping to the completed stalk and identifying that completed stalk with the one of a crossing model.
